# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example — copy to `.env` (gitignored) to set the DeepSeek key and/or tune
# defaults:  cp .env.example .env
#
#   • OpenAI/Codex (the Reviewer) → run `codex login` (browser OAuth), NOT this file.
#   • DeepSeek key (optional, for cheap builds) → DEEPSEEK_API_KEY below, OR an env
#     var, OR ~/.fcc/.env. With no key the Carpenter just builds on Anthropic Claude.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# DeepSeek key — routes the default `claude` Carpenter to DeepSeek's Anthropic
# endpoint (cheap builds, NO free-claude-code router; ADR-0012). Omit to build on
# Anthropic Claude. Get one at https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
#   Override the endpoint if you proxy DeepSeek elsewhere (default shown).
# SHIP_DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic
#   Model the DeepSeek-routed Worker requests. opus -> deepseek-v4-pro (quality, default),
#   haiku -> deepseek-v4-flash (fast/cheap). Only haiku maps to flash.
# SHIP_CARPENTER_MODEL=opus

# Token cap across all rounds before the loop escalates (default 2,000,000).
# SHIP_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000

# Engine overrides (ADR-0004 / ADR-0012). Each role is a headless CLI command;
# swap any of them without editing ship.js. Defaults shown.
#   Carpenter (Worker) — default `claude` (→ DeepSeek when DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is set).
#   Set to `fcc-claude` to use the legacy free-claude-code router instead.
# SHIP_CARPENTER_CMD=claude
#   Master Carpenter (foreman) — inspects the Worker's build. Default: claude.
# SHIP_MASTER_CMD=claude
#   Reviewer — independent auditor. Default: codex.
# SHIP_REVIEWER_CMD=codex

# Worker Carpenter effort tier (ADR-0010). 'ultracode' is NOT a valid value — it's a
# mode (xhigh effort + dynamic-workflow orchestration). We force the safe effort half.
#   Valid: low | medium | high | xhigh | max.  Default: xhigh.  Set to "" to disable.
# SHIP_CARPENTER_EFFORT=xhigh
#   Opt into the dynamic-workflow half (the "workflow" part of ultracode). Guarded:
#   the loop blocks worktree isolation so sub-agents build in-tree, and halts loudly
#   (never a silent no-op) if one isolates anyway. Safe to enable; effect unverified.
# SHIP_CARPENTER_WORKFLOW=1
